### AI Model Weights over IP Multicast
*Presented by Ead and Omar Ramadan*  
*Slides:* [AI model weights over IP multicast](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mboned-ai-model-weights-over-ip-multicast-00)

* **Use Case:** Transferring large AI model weights (e.g., Qwen2.5-3B, ~6.18 GB) across edge cache nodes and compute clusters.
* **Implementation:** Uses IP multicast combined with Reed-Solomon Forward Error Correction (10 data + 2 parity packets = 20% parity block overhead) and in-band range NACK retries.
* **Results:** Multicast outperformed unicast across all bandwidth caps (450 Mbps to 1 Gbps). Multicast total egress bandwidth remained constant regardless of receiver node count.
* **Discussion:**
  * Jake Holland drew parallels to NORM; Omar noted similarities to MoDE with in-band NACKs.
  * Toerless Eckert discussed cloud and data center economics, highlighting how multicasting model updates reduces compute worker idle time during model distribution.
  * Mike McBride encouraged the authors to submit their findings as an MBONED Internet-Draft.

