### Dynamic Internet Multicast Tunneling
*Presented by Mike McBride*  
*Slides:* [Dynamic Internet Multicast Tunneling](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mboned-dynamic-internet-multicast-tunneling-00)

* **Concept:** Provides zero-configuration, dynamic middle-mile tunneling (e.g., AMT or GRE) across non-multicast transit networks between autonomous systems.
* **Updates:** 
  * Replaced the previously proposed BGP Extended Community with a new BGP Attribute to carry AMT relay discovery information without risk of BGP filtering across inter-domain boundaries.
  * Routers perform Reverse Path Forwarding (RPF) lookups on the source IP, discover the relay address in the BGP attribute, and dynamically establish an AMT tunnel.
* **Discussion:**
  * In chat, Jake Holland noted similarities to `draft-jholland-idr-mcast-source-nexthop-over-amt`. Lenny Giuliano and Greg Shepherd noted that extending BGP attributes will require coordination with the IDR working group.
  * The authors plan to update the draft after the IETF submission blackout lifts.

