### FEC with MoQ (over Multicast)
*Presented by Dirk Trossen*  
*Slides:* [FEC with MoQ (over multicast)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mboned-fec-with-moq-over-multicast-00)

* **Architecture:** Applies receiver-driven layered multicast FEC concepts to Media over QUIC (MoQ). Repair tracks are published as distinct MoQ tracks.
* **Operation:** Subscribers choose how many FEC repair tracks to join based on local path loss. Relays remain entirely FEC-agnostic, keeping middleboxes simple.
* **Implementation:** Tested on Unicast MoQ and ported to PicoQUIC / QUICcast as part of an open-source initiative.
* **Discussion:**
  * Francois Michel and Jake Holland noted that application-layer FEC in MoQ provides significant delay advantages over lossy or bursty networks without requiring modifications to the core QUIC transport.

